<title>USA: Pa. company wins $100 mln New York City waste deal.</title>
<headline>Pa. company wins $100 mln New York City waste deal.</headline>
<dateline>PENN TOWNSHIP, Pa. 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Lancaster County, Pa., company won a nearly $100 million contract to composte New York City waste.</p>
<p>J-P Mascaro and Sons of Harleysville will process 156 tons of sludge a day for the next 15 years as part of the $95.6 million deal.</p>
<p>The company's composting plant near Manheim will begin getting seven or eight truckloads of sludge a day beginning in July of 1998.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
